## Example Input Structure

The input is a JSON array containing objects such as:

- `directory`: describes a directory and its contents
- `report`: summarizes counts like number of directories and files
- `instructions`: contains code change instructions

Example:

```json
[
    {
        "type": "directory",
        "name": ".",
        "contents": [
            {
                "type": "file",
                "name": "README.md",
                "content": "This is the README.md file content"
            },
            {
                "type": "file",
                "name": "system.md",
                "content": "This is the system.md file contents"
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "type": "report",
        "directories": 1,
        "files": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "instructions",
        "name": "code_change_instructions",
        "details": "Update README and refactor main.py"
    }
]
```

The `instructions` object always has:

- `type`: `"instructions"`
- `name`: `"code_change_instructions"`
- `details`: the suggested code changes

## Interactivity Requirements

The HTML document must support the following interactive behavior:

- **Fix node on drag end**
  ```js
  network.on("dragEnd", (params) => {
      if (params.nodes.length > 0) {
          nodes.update({ id: params.nodes[0], fixed: true });
      }
  });
  ```

- **Release node on double click**
  ```js
  network.on("doubleClick", (params) => {
      if (params.nodes.length > 0) {
          nodes.update({ id: params.nodes[0], fixed: false });
      }
  });
  ```

