## Component Changes: Search Filtering Logic

Introduce a `searchText` variable and use it to filter patterns before sorting.

```typescript
// Add to script section
let searchText = ""; // For pattern filtering

// Modify sortedPatterns to include search
$: filteredPatterns = patterns.filter(p => 
  p.patternName.toLowerCase().includes(searchText.toLowerCase())
);

$: sortedPatterns = sortBy === 'alphabetical'
  ? [...filteredPatterns].sort((a, b) => a.patternName.localeCompare(b.patternName))
  : [
      ...filteredPatterns.filter(p => $favorites.includes(p.patternName)).sort((a, b) => a.patternName.localeCompare(b.patternName)),
      ...filteredPatterns.filter(p => !$favorites.includes(p.patternName)).sort((a, b) => a.patternName.localeCompare(b.patternName))
    ];
```

This ensures searching happens first, and sorting is applied to the filtered list.

## Component Changes: Reset Search on Selection

Clear the search text when a pattern is selected, before closing the modal.

```typescript
// In pattern selection click handler
searchText = ""; // Reset search before closing modal
dispatch('select', pattern.patternName);
dispatch('close');
```

This prevents the previous search term from persisting after a selection.

## Setting Up Mdsvex in SvelteKit

To use these examples, the SvelteKit project must be configured to support Mdsvex.

### 1. Install Mdsvex

```bash
npm install -D mdsvex
```

### 2. Configure `svelte.config.js`

```javascript
import adapter from '@sveltejs/adapter-auto';
import { vitePreprocess } from '@sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte';
import { mdsvex } from 'mdsvex';

/** @type {import('mdsvex').MdsvexOptions} */
const mdsvexOptions = {
  extensions: ['.svx'],
};

/** @type {import('@sveltejs/kit').Config} */
const config = {
  extensions: ['.svelte', '.svx'],
  preprocess: [
    vitePreprocess(),
    mdsvex(mdsvexOptions),
  ],
  kit: {
    adapter: adapter()
  }
};

export default config;
```

Important configuration details:
- Add `.svx` to the list of supported extensions.
- Use `mdsvex(mdsvexOptions)` in the preprocessing pipeline.
- Keep Svelte preprocessing via `vitePreprocess()`.

## Drawer Interaction and Page Behavior

```svelte
<script>
  import { Button } from '$lib/components/ui/button';
  import NoteDrawer from '$lib/components/ui/noteDrawer/NoteDrawer.svelte';
  import { getDrawerStore } from '@skeletonlabs/skeleton';
  import { page } from '$app/stores';
  import { beforeNavigate } from '$app/navigation';

  const drawerStore = getDrawerStore();
  function openDrawer() {
    drawerStore.open({});
  }

  beforeNavigate(() => {
    drawerStore.close();
  });

  $: isVisible = $page.url.pathname.startsWith('/welcome');
</script>
```

This code sets up a drawer UI using Skeleton Labs' drawer store. The `openDrawer()` function opens the drawer, and `beforeNavigate()` ensures the drawer closes when navigating away. The `isVisible` reactive value checks whether the current path starts with `/welcome`.
